\begin_layout Standard
Firstly we notice that for fixed 
\begin_inset Formula $o,c$
\end_inset

 the number of times 
\begin_inset Formula $p_{\theta}\left(o|c\right)$
\end_inset

 shows in the objective is 
\begin_inset Formula $\#\left(c,o\right)$
\end_inset

,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This follows from the fact that in each window where both 
\begin_inset Formula $o,c$
\end_inset

 is in we count 
\begin_inset Formula $p_{\theta}\left(o|c\right)$
\end_inset

 one more time.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\mathcal{L}\left(\left(c,o\right),\theta\right)=\#\left(c,o\right)\log\left(p_{\theta}\left(o|c\right)\right)
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For a fixed 
\begin_inset Formula $o,c$
\end_inset

 we must make sure 
\begin_inset Formula $\sum_{o'\in Voc}p_{\theta}\left(o'|c\right)=1$
\end_inset

 namely 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta$
\end_inset

 is a probability distribution.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Therefore we will use Lagrange multiplier with 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda$
\end_inset

 parameter to enforce this constraint.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We want to find the following 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta^{*}$
\end_inset

:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\theta^{*}=\arg\max_{\theta}\mathcal{L}\left(\theta\right)=\arg\max_{\theta}\mathcal{L}\left(\left(c,o\right),\lambda,\theta\right)=\#\left(c,o\right)\log\left(p_{\theta}\left(o|c\right)\right)+\lambda-\lambda\sum_{o'\in Voc}p_{\theta}\left(o|c\right)
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Differentiating by 
\begin_inset Formula $p_{\theta}\left(o|c\right)$
\end_inset

 and comparing to 
\begin_inset Formula $0$
\end_inset

 we get:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\frac{d\mathcal{L}\left(\mathcal{L}\left(\left(c,o\right),\lambda,\theta\right)\right)}{dp} & =\frac{\#\left(c,o\right)}{p_{\theta}\left(o|c\right)}-\lambda=0\\
p_{\theta}\left(o|c\right) & =\frac{\#\left(c,o\right)}{\lambda}
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Now substitute back into the original Lagrange multiplier definition:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\sum_{o'\in Voc}p_{\theta}\left(o'|c\right) & =\sum_{o'\in Voc}\frac{\#\left(c,o'\right)}{\lambda}=1\\
\lambda & =\sum_{o'\in Voc}\#\left(c,o'\right)
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

